# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Config, not content.
#
# Cache-Control is deliberately NOT set here: Pages manages caching for its own
# assets and ignores the directive from this file. Verified — the two headers
# below take effect on the same responses where a Cache-Control line did not.
# The stylesheet's TTL is fixed by a response-header Transform Rule on the
# zone instead; Assets/Web/README.md records it and why it has to live there.
#
# Applied to everything. Cheap, and they are worth having regardless.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
